            <ArticleTitle>Too little mTORC1 activity injures the liver.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>4-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.cmet.2014.06.005</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1550-4131(14)00270-8</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Obesity promotes chronic activation of mTORC1 and is a known risk factor for hepatic injury, inflammation, and carcinogenesis. In this issue, Umemura et al. (2014) demonstrate that a persistent reduction in hepatic mTORC1 activity also promotes cell damage and inflammation and sensitizes the liver to cancer development.</AbstractText>
